      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Alabama-Georgia Manufacturing Company, founded in 1866 by George Huguley, was the region’s first cotton mill and employed hundreds along the Chattahoochee River.",
